  "necessity_assessment": {
    "hard_compatibility_knowledge": "Necessary for constructing callable candidates and predicting direct, adapt and fallback execution; it transfers across the tested hosts.",
    "packing_and_call_contract": "Critical. Removing the packing rule reduces the formal normalized geometric mean from 0.800 to 0.046.",
    "fixed_source_performance_constants": "Not generally necessary or safe as hard constraints. The no-MR/NR ablation reaches 0.962, and the f64 candidate-pool ranking reverses relative to complete BLIS across hosts.",
    "calibrated_soft_prior": "Target-data calibration improves low-budget selection over no-prior search, but the termination ablation finds no statistically supported increment from the current BLIS-derived soft performance features. Its 591-row calibration cost also does not amortize within 12 holdouts."
  },
  "main_conclusion": "The defensible contribution is a compiler workflow that turns transferable hard compatibility knowledge into callable direct/adapt schedules and extends to a second BLIS microkernel Contract without changing the core space generator. Within the frozen 28-candidate measured subpools, BaCO does not outperform uniform random search without replacement. Target data can improve low-budget search in the separate calibrated-prior experiments, but the current BLIS-derived soft performance rules add no demonstrated value beyond that data and their measured calibration cost is not practically amortized in the frozen horizon.",
  "current_boundaries": [
    "Single-thread row-major GEMM remains the main x86 evaluation boundary.",
    "Arbitrary layouts, strides, transposes and batched operators are not covered.",
    "K230 evidence is limited to one physical C908 RT-Smart board and toolchain.",
    "The two-host x86 result does not establish universal host-independent ranking.",
    "Chapter 5 speedups use a scalar-loop dynamic fallback; complete-library comparisons are reported separately.",
    "No end-to-end model or application-level speedup is claimed.",
    "The Qwen trace is model-code coverage evidence; the i7 WSL exact-shape timing pool failed qualification and is excluded from performance claims.",
    "The second microkernel is on the same BLIS Haswell backend; independent-backend extensibility is not established."
  ],
  "publication_extensions": [
    "Add another independent x86 or RISC-V target and preserve the same fixed-budget protocol.",
    "Evaluate multithreaded execution and hardware counters for packing, cache and memory effects.",
    "Extend Contracts to layout/stride/transpose/batched GEMM cases.",
    "Evaluate one end-to-end operator or model workload without weakening the current baselines.",
    "Replace the explicit two-entry runtime registry with a descriptor-driven independent-backend package and test it on a distinct library or ISA."
